.TH NNNYAZ 1 "2026-11-20" "nnnyaz 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nnnyaz \- a small nnn/Yazi-style terminal file manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nnnyaz
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nnnyaz
is a modal terminal file manager. It combines nnn's startup flags and picker
mode with Yazi-style keymaps, tabs, marks, a trash bin, a task manager, and a
native preview pane for text, images, PDFs, archives, and media.
.PP
Configuration is read from
.IR $NNNYAZ_CONFIG_HOME ,
then
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/nnnyaz ,
then
.IR ~/.config/nnnyaz .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-generate\-config
Print a commented default
.IR config.toml
to stdout and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Report configuration warnings and exit with status 1 if any were found.
.TP
.BI \-\-cwd-file= PATH
Write the current directory to
.I PATH
when quitting with
.BR Q .
.TP
.BI \-\-chooser-file= PATH
Picker mode: write chosen paths to
.IR PATH .
Use
.B \-
to write to stdout.
.TP
.BI \-p " PATH"
Alias for
.BR \-\-chooser-file .
.TP
.BR \-0 ", " \-\-null
Separate picker paths with NUL instead of newlines.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-hidden
Show hidden files at startup.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-file-info
Show the hovered file's type in the status line.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-detail
Start with the detail linemode.
.TP
.BR \-U ", " \-\-owner
Start with the owner linemode.
.TP
.BR \-J ", " \-\-no-auto-advance
Keep the cursor on an entry after toggling its selection.
.TP
.BI \-b " KEY" ", " \-\-bookmark= KEY
Start in a bookmark. Ignored if
.I PATH
is given.
.TP
.BR \-Q ", " \-\-no-confirm-quit
Quit without warning about running tasks.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-open-on-enter
Only Enter opens files;
.B l
and right-arrow only enter directories.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-type-to-nav
Start in nnn-style type-to-nav mode.
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-no-autoenter
Do not auto-enter a lone matching directory.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-regex
Use regex filters.
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-fuzzy
Use fuzzy filters.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-editor
Open text files in
.IR $VISUAL ,
then
.IR $EDITOR ,
then
.BR vi .
.TP
.BR \-E ", " \-\-internal-editor
Use
.I $EDITOR
for internal edits such as bulk rename.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cli-opener
Run
.I $NNN_OPENER
attached to the terminal; this trumps
.BR \-e .
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-history
Keep a persistent shell command history.
.TP
.BR \-K ", " \-\-key-collisions
Report keymap collisions and exit.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-use-selection
Accepted for nnn compatibility; nnnyaz always uses the selection.
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-no-rollover
Accepted for nnn compatibility.
.TP
.BI \-s " NAME" ", " \-\-session= NAME
Load a session;
.B @
means the last session.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-persistent-session
Save the session on exit.
.TP
.BI \-T " KEY" ", " \-\-sort= KEY
Sort order:
.BR a / d / s
by name, natural, or size;
.B e
by extension;
.B t
by time;
.B v
natural. An uppercase key reverses the order.
.TP
.BI \-l " N" ", " \-\-scroll= N
Lines moved per mouse-wheel step. Default: 1.
.TP
.BI \-t " N" ", " \-\-lock-after= N
Lock the terminal after
.I N
idle seconds. Use 0 to disable.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.I NNNYAZ_CWD_FILE
Default for
.BR \-\-cwd-file .
.TP
.I NNNYAZ_CHOOSER_FILE
Default for
.BR \-\-chooser-file .
.TP
.I NNNYAZ_CONFIG_HOME
Configuration directory.
.TP
.I NNNYAZ_IMAGE_PROTOCOL
Force
.BR kitty ,
.BR sixel ,
or
.BR none .
.TP
.I NNN_LOCKER
Terminal locker for
.BR \-t ;
default
.BR vlock .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/nnnyaz/config.toml
Main configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/nnnyaz/keymap.toml
Keymaps.
.TP
.I ~/.config/nnnyaz/theme.toml
Theme roles.
.TP
.I ~/.config/nnnyaz/init.lua
Optional Lua overrides.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nnn (1),
.BR yazi (1)
